  "id": "Enfield-25_01601_CEA",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed rear extension, by reason of measuring more than half the width of the original property, would not constitute Permitted Development under Article 3 and Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (as amended)",
    "Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the proposal would fall within use class C3b of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended). In particular no information has been provided in relation to the proposed staffing arrangements - including number of staff, whether they will reside at the property, whether they would work in shifts and what those shift patterns may be. In the absence of such information, it is not possible to confirm that the proposed use would fall within use class C3b or whether a material change of use would have occurred. The proposal as submitted has therefore failed to demonstrate that it would fall within Use Class C3(b), and as such, the Lawful Development Certificate cannot be granted."
  ],
